        "title": "Installing with pip",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Use packages others created",
            "id": 151738,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We've learned that a module is just a Python file that can be shared, imported, and reused. Multiple modules can form a package.</p><p>We can use a package someone else created. Let's learn how to install and import Python packages to do that.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = [\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Alice&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Bob&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"30\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(tabulate.tabulate(data))\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"-----  --\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Alice  25\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Bob    30\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"-----  --\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare code sources",
            "id": 151739,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Python includes many useful modules in its standard library, while additional functionality is available through third-party packages.</p><p>Python provides packages, such as <code>math</code>, <code>random</code>, etc., which we can use to extend its functionality.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" random\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" math\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(random.randint(\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"))\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(math.sqrt(\" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"install\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"9\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"4.0\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>, followed by <code>import</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Python includes many useful modules in its standard library, while additional functionality is available through third-party packages.</p><p>Python provides packages, such as <code>math</code>, <code>random</code>, etc., which we can use to extend its functionality.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" random\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" math\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(random.randint(\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"))\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(math.sqrt(\" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"from\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"install\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"randint\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"9\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"4.0\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>, followed by <code>import</code>, and finally <code>sqrt</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare code sources - Copy",
            "id": 151765,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can further extend Python’s functionality with third-party packages created by other developers, such as <code>tabulate</code>.</p><p>We always use the same import keyword. Complete the keyword that imports the third-party package.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" random\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" math\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"install\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Read the error",
            "id": 151740,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unlike standard library modules, third-party packages usually need to be installed before you can use them.<br /><br /></p><p><code>ModuleNotFoundError</code> commonly means Python can't find the requested module. Importing alone is not enough here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" random\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" math\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"41\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"install\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tabulate'\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>, followed by <code>tabulate</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Use the command line",
            "id": 151766,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><strong>pip</strong> is Python's package installer. At the command line, <code>pip</code> starts that installer.</p><p>Complete the command-line tool shown here. You'll learn what <code>pip</code> does next.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"import\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Meet pip",
            "id": 151743,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><strong>Installing</strong> adds a package to an environment. Only then can we import it and make it available to a program.</p><p>After <code>pip</code>, we write <code>install</code> to trigger the install command of the package manager.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"import\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Add the package name",
            "id": 151745,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>pip install</code>, <code>pip</code> starts the installer and <code>install</code> tells it to add something.</p><p>A package name follows <code>pip install</code>. Complete the package name <code>tabulate</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"random\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Collecting tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Downloading tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Installing collected packages: tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Successfully installed tabulate\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>tabulate</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A package name follows the installation command.</p><p>Use the installer to add the table-formatting package <code>tabulate</code> to your environment.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"import\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"random\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"tabulate.py\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Collecting tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Downloading tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Installing collected packages: tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Successfully installed tabulate\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>, and finally <code>tabulate</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Complete pip install",
            "id": 151746,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the action in the command. The full command asks pip to add <code>tabulate</code> to the environment.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"import\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>install</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the action in the command. The full command asks pip to add <code>tabulate</code> to the environment.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"include\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"require\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"helpers\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>, and finally <code>tabulate</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Identify third-party code",
            "id": 151747,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Assume <code>data_tools</code> is already installed. Complete the keyword that imports this installed third-party package.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" data_tools\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"install\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Assume <code>data_tools</code> is already installed. Complete the keyword that imports this installed third-party package.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" data_tools\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"require\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"helpers\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"script\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>import</code>, followed by <code>data_tools</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Choose the next action",
            "id": 151748,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>An import raises <code>ModuleNotFoundError</code> because its third-party package is missing. What should happen before trying again?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Install the missing package in the environment</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Write the same import again</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Install the missing package in the environment.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>import tabulate</code> fails because the package is missing. Which command-line step lets you retry the same import?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Run pip install tabulate in the environment.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Run import tabulate again without installing it.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Run pip install math and keep import tabulate.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Run pip install tabulate in the environment.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
