      {
        "id": 17788,
        "title": "Using Requirements Files",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Share the package list",
            "id": 151751,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When pip installs a package, it adds the package to the active environment. An environment is the Python setup currently used to run code.</p><p>A coworker or coding agent uses another environment. Without the same packages, the code can't run.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = [\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Alice&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Vienna&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Bob&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"30\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Berlin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Charlie&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"28\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;London&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"],\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(tabulate.tabulate(data, headers=[\" /><text value=\"&quot;Name&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Age&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;City&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]))\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Name       Age  City\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"-------  -----  ------\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Alice       25  Vienna\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Bob         30  Berlin\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Charlie     28  London\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Share the package list - Copy",
            "id": 151781,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Python offers a solution with <code>requirements.txt</code>, a text file that lists the packages a project needs.<br /></p><p>In the <code>requirements.txt</code> file, we specify all the third-party packages we need.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"random\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>tabulate</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Share the package list - Copy 2",
            "id": 151782,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Each line names one required package. We can use as many as we need/want.</p><p>We don't list <code>random</code> or <code>math</code> in <code>requirements.txt</code>, even if we use them, because they are part of Python’s standard library.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"text\" name=\"requirements.txt\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"requests\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"flask\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"pandas\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"numpy\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare install commands",
            "id": 151755,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Similar to installing a single package with <code>pip</code>, we can install all packages listed in <code>requirements.txt</code> at once.</p><p>Start with <code>pip install</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"python\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Read the full command",
            "id": 151756,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>pip install -r requirements.txt</code>, the familiar <code>pip install</code> starts the installation action.</p><p>The flag <code>-r</code> makes <code>pip</code> aware that what follows is not a package to install but a list of requirements. Then, we specify the file name.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install -r requirements.txt\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"31\" /><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Collecting requests\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting flask\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting pandas\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting numpy\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Installing collected packages: requests, flask, pandas, numpy, tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Successfully installed requests flask pandas numpy tabulate\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pip</code>, followed by <code>install</code>, and finally <code>-r requirements.txt</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Understand the -r option",
            "id": 151757,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>-r</code> option tells <code>pip</code> to read package requirements from a file instead of one package name.</p><p>Complete the option before the filename. It changes how the command works.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"bash\" name=\"script.sh\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"pip install -r requirements.txt\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"14\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Collecting requests\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting flask\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting pandas\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting numpy\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Collecting tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Installing collected packages: requests, flask, pandas, numpy, tabulate\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Successfully installed requests flask pandas numpy tabulate\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>-r</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Dependency",
            "id": 151829,
